219 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (During the duration of the piece, the performers build an everyday scene from an old house: A rug, a wooden chair, a lamp and a series of small ceramic objects that fill the space. As the performance unfolds, a spectral presence begins to manifest. The on-screen world drifts away from the tangible reality of the stage. Objects seemingly move of their own accord, and sounds become dislocated from their sources. This ghostly manifestation defies logical connections, causing the distinct stage materials to begin to merge.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
